name issue_62_neteq_v2_audio_only_lossy
describe audio_only_lossy with NetEq's operations (neteq v2, issue #62): play from the first packet, preemptive expand up to the target
duration 30s
video off
neteq v2
at 0s capacity=500kbps delay=40ms jitter=10ms loss=10%
# libwebrtc M157 on audio_only_lossy (compare-webrtc, seeds 1-10): jitter buffer
# delay p95 70-90 ms, mouth-to-ear p95 133-168 ms. neteq v2 with v1's operations
# (#213): 60 ms and 133 ms on seeds 1-5; with DecisionLogic: 72 ms and 145 ms.
expect audio.interruptions == 0
expect audio.concealed_pct < 3
expect audio.jb_delay_p95_ms >= 66
expect audio.mouth_to_ear_p95_ms >= 139
# PR for #457 (libopus 55513e81 replaces the Opus size model; program.md 0.2, needs-human): was <= 170. Ours 175.3 on seed 1
# (seeds 1-10 133-175, mean 153); libwebrtc seeds 1-10 143-171 (mean 161), and sm_compare's own side of this library already 177
# on seed 10 on main's compare-webrtc. Seed-1 outlier; mean in band (ours 153.1 / libwebrtc 160.6, seeds 1-10, band 8.0):
# 10 % above seed 1 (175.3 x 1.10), the outlier clause (Coordinator on the PR for #457).
expect audio.mouth_to_ear_p95_ms <= 193
# Opus in-band FEC on the receive side (#62 step 7): libwebrtc M157 conceals 0.27-0.67 % on seeds 1-10
# (mean 0.46). Ours with LBRR: 0.33-0.50 % on seeds 1-8 and 10, 1.24 on seed 9; without it 0.77-2.10 (seed 1 0.94).
# Issue #507 (the harness hands each packet to the stack at its arrival time and sends the response then, as
# sm_compare's libwebrtc side; program.md 0.2, a harness change that makes the sides more alike): was < 0.7. Ours on
# audio_only_lossy seeds 1-10 0.28-0.76 (mean 0.527, was 0.475; seed 1 0.705, was 0.474); libwebrtc M157 on
# compare-webrtc seeds 1-10 0.282 0.297 0.356 0.445 0.459 0.491 0.503 0.534 0.755 0.963 (mean 0.509). Worst seed 0.963.
# PR for #518 merged with main after #543 and #551 (harness: timers at their due microsecond, the sides more alike;
# program.md 0.2's exception, up to libwebrtc's worst seed): was < 0.75. Ours seeds 1-10 0.840 0.390 0.387 0.184 0.639
# 0.531 0.714 0.357 0.729 0.333 (mean 0.510; main's test bench seed 1 0.442); libwebrtc seeds 1-10 0.963 0.491 0.297 0.282
# 0.445 0.534 0.755 0.503 0.459 0.356 (mean 0.509). Seed-1 outlier, mean in band: 10 % above seed 1 (0.84 x 1.10), below
# libwebrtc's worst seed 0.963.
# PR for #813 (pacer as libwebrtc's TaskQueuePacedSender/PacerConfig, a stage-1 port; program.md 0.2, needs-human): was < 0.93.
# audio_only_lossy seed 1 is now packet for packet libwebrtc's forward link (2357 packets), and libwebrtc conceals 0.963 there.
# Ours seeds 1-10 0.943 0.246 0.297 0.287 0.439 0.420 0.755 0.462 0.460 0.380 (mean 0.473); libwebrtc seeds 1-10 0.963 0.491
# 0.297 0.282 0.445 0.534 0.755 0.503 0.459 0.356 (mean 0.509). Line at libwebrtc's worst seed.
expect audio.concealed_pct < 0.964
